From 40fa331c0b36b9b7bb6ccc07d27eaaca1875581f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allcodernet <67543055+allcodernet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:14:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/45] decide-compat: bound nesting, size and question count;
 status from map_decide_error

systemone_to_decide checks the nesting depth of state, instructions and
every criteria value before it serialises them: deeper than 32 levels is
a 422 at the value's loc. Pretty text grows with the square of the
depth, so a small request could build gigabytes of text or overflow the
stack in the recursive serialiser. The text built from request values is
capped at 2 MiB per request (422 at ["body"]), more than 64 questions is
a 422 at ["body","questions"] before any question is translated, and an
empty state is a 422 at ["body","state"] instead of the compiler's
states error at ["body"]. The built fields and states move into the
result.

map_decide_error_body becomes map_decide_error and returns the status
with the body (budget 400, other post-task 400s 422); the /v1/systemone
route uses it. compat_error derives from std::runtime_error, so what()
gives the message if one escapes a handler.

test-decide-compat: case 4 compares text() with literal strings (UTF-8
kept), case 10 asserts both statuses, case 12 covers the bounds (depth
33 rejected at the loc of state, instructions, a choice value, a score
entry and a noul half; depth 32 accepted; 65 questions; empty state; the
2 MiB total for one value and across values). test-decide-trie asserts
error.field on the sale/sales sibling conflict.
